--TEST--
An isolate shares nothing with its *siblings* either: the same child spawned five times reads the fresh store every time, so a store is built for each child rather than reused between them — ADR 0006 § *Decision*, `rule:statements/an-isolate-has-its-own-statics`
--FILE nvs.toml--
# `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`: `spawn script` goes through a door that asks for
# `script.spawn` first. This grants it and nothing else.
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE child.nvs--
<?nvs
// One child, spawned five times by the parent below. It reports the store it
// was given and then writes over it, so a store carried from one child to the
// next would show up twice: in the line this echoes and in what it returns.
final class Tally {
    public static int $runs = 0;
}

echo Tally::$runs;
Tally::$runs = Tally::$runs + 1;
return Tally::$runs;
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/a-child-shares-nothing
// The sweep shape rather than the single read: five children, one assertion
// over all of them. A runtime that built the statics base once and handed the
// same one to every child still prints `1` for the first child, so a case
// reading one line cannot tell the two apart — these two counts can.

final class Tally {
    public static int $runs = 0;
}

// The parent writes its own store first. It is the one thing in this program a
// child could reach if statics crossed the boundary at all.
Tally::$runs = 100;

uint $fresh = 0;
uint $total = 0;
uint $i = 0;
while ($i < 5) {
    var $handle = spawn script "child.nvs" with(output: "capture");
    var $done = await $handle;
    $total = $total + ($done->value as uint);
    if ($done->output == "0") {
        $fresh = $fresh + 1;
    }
    $i = $i + 1;
}

// Both counts are the assertion. `5 of 5` says no child read what an earlier
// one wrote; a total of 5 rather than 15 says each `return` answered 1, which
// only holds when the store behind it was built for that child alone.
echo "fresh: ", $fresh, " of 5\n";
echo "total: ", $total, "\n";
echo "the parent still reads ", Tally::$runs, "\n";
--EXPECT--
fresh: 5 of 5
total: 5
the parent still reads 100
